          "studentExplanation": "Bertha Benz’s 1888 journey in Germany helped prove that the automobile could be useful beyond short demonstrations. But the road trip became especially powerful in the United States because roads, cars, distance, tourism, migration, and ideas of freedom all came together. The American road trip is not just a drive; it became a national story about space, independence, discovery, and self-direction.\n\nBertha Benz proves long car travel before the American myth, but the United States made the road trip culturally central through distance, highways, motels, cars, migration, music, and ideas of freedom. The road trip is infrastructure plus story. Use this to treat roads as systems, not background: what the route is built to do, where it channels people or goods, how it changes choices, and why routes remain cultural even after their practical role changes.",
